ens, with the 10 on the board acting as the kicker. The river paired the King, creating a board of 5s, Qs, 10h, Kh, Kc. The opponent has checked to me on the river. Betting here is risky because worse hands (like a pair of 10s or 5s) will likely fold, while better hands (Trips, Straights, or a Queen with a better kicker like A or J) will call or raise. Since I am currently in the lead in the overall match (Hand 18/20) and have showdown value, checking back minimizes risk and secures the pot if my hand is best without exposing me to a check-raise.\n\nReason: My hand has showdown value but limited value for betting, as worse hands fold and better hands call. Checking guarantees I see the showdown for free, preserving my chip lead.\n\nAnswer: 0'}
